WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.752
- We're not ones to fall and stay on the ground.

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:04.004
We get up.

00:00:06.548 --> 00:00:08.800
We're going to show y'all
what one love really means.

00:00:09.426 --> 00:00:12.762
- We are going to disturb all the
stereotypes that they think about us.

00:00:12.929 --> 00:00:18.268
We are going to disturb all the people that
say, "I'm not Black so it's not my problem."

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:22.313
- Basketball is something that really
allows people to come together

00:00:22.313 --> 00:00:23.898
no matter what background you are.

00:00:24.232 --> 00:00:28.153
- It just creates a good form to open up
conversation and create a bond right away.

00:00:28.486 --> 00:00:30.155
- We're disturbing that here today.

00:00:30.155 --> 00:00:31.865
We're disturbing that here tomorrow.

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:34.951
And we're disturbing that here
for the rest of our lives.

00:00:44.127 --> 00:00:47.797
- The job that I do is like I'm a community
activist and a basketball architect,

00:00:47.797 --> 00:00:52.260
and I always try to evolve like James
Naismith's vision for basketball.

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:57.182
The Hoop Bus is something that was
cooking on my brain for about 10 years.

00:00:57.182 --> 00:01:02.062
What if we kind of renovated a school bus and
turned it into a basketball traveling machine.

00:01:02.479 --> 00:01:06.274
Found this beautiful bus collecting
dust in the middle of the Palm Desert.

00:01:06.691 --> 00:01:12.280
- Their mission is to rebuild basketball courts all
over the country with a message to end racism.

00:01:12.864 --> 00:01:16.159
- The entire mission of the Hoop
Bus is to bring people together.

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:19.621
- Uniting them through basketball, art and fashion.

00:01:19.996 --> 00:01:23.833
- We felt called to dedicate the bus
to the Black Lives Matter movement.

00:01:24.209 --> 00:01:26.669
- I have faced racial injustice in America.

00:01:26.961 --> 00:01:28.546
I have been racially profiled.

00:01:28.797 --> 00:01:34.928
I have been falsely accused and arrested and
gone to jail and had to fight for my freedom.

00:01:35.011 --> 00:01:36.304
So I know what it feels like.

00:01:36.471 --> 00:01:41.559
- We all have this message that we want to get
across—a message of positivity, a message of love.

00:01:41.893 --> 00:01:48.858
- We are basically the Freedom Riders of 2020.

00:01:48.858 --> 00:01:54.072
- The idea for the road trip was sparked by our goal
of traveling the country and building communities.

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:58.284
The March on Washington, which was
publicized after the killing of George Floyd,

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:02.205
for us felt like a monumental
task that we could build towards.

00:02:02.705 --> 00:02:05.750
- In each one of these stops, we're
going to be spreading a message of

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:07.418
love and unity through basketball.

00:02:07.669 --> 00:02:09.337
We want to do what we've done in L.A.

00:02:09.379 --> 00:02:10.505
and spread it across the country.

00:02:11.172 --> 00:02:15.885
- We want to come show support and solidarity and
start connecting and start having conversation

00:02:15.927 --> 00:02:20.682
and just realize that really basketball
is the common story, and it really unites.

00:02:21.057 --> 00:02:25.478
For this tour we installed bunk
beds, outdoor showers, AC system.

00:02:25.687 --> 00:02:28.231
We replaced the indoors with hardwood floors.

00:02:28.356 --> 00:02:32.277
We changed the seating area so people can
face each other and it's more conversational.

00:02:32.694 --> 00:02:36.197
For a project like this to come together,
it's all about the people involved.

00:02:36.281 --> 00:02:39.117
- The diversity amongst us is phenomenal.

00:02:39.117 --> 00:02:41.828
We have people from every different background.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.997
- We've been almost all the
way across the country now.

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:45.373
- Starting off in L.A.

00:02:45.415 --> 00:02:48.001
where the Hoop Bus originated,
Venice Beach, California.

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:51.004
- Hit Redlands for a small protest, Palm Springs.

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:53.381
- Phoenix, Arizona; Albuquerque, New Mexico.

00:02:53.548 --> 00:02:54.340
- Dallas, Texas.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:55.508
We went to Houston, Texas.

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:57.093
- Went to New Orleans on Bourbon Street.

00:02:57.427 --> 00:02:57.594
- Batesville.

00:02:57.594 --> 00:03:00.138
- We went to Birmingham; Atlanta, Georgia.

00:03:00.221 --> 00:03:03.683
- Charlotte, North Carolina; Raleigh,
North Carolina; then Washington, D.C.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:06.686
- This is an event that was kind of
announced through social media.

00:03:06.936 --> 00:03:09.731
Even in small towns where it's like a
hundred or 200 people, people already

00:03:09.772 --> 00:03:11.524
know about the Hoop Bus is incredible.

00:03:12.066 --> 00:03:14.736
It's already become this, like, vehicle of change.

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:20.742
- One of the main things on our
trip was improving courts.

00:03:21.451 --> 00:03:23.745
- One of my favorite moments was in Dallas.

00:03:23.745 --> 00:03:27.207
We built a court for a
community, and it was phenomenal.

00:03:27.332 --> 00:03:31.586
- Like these guys really came to our community,
our little community where nobody comes,

00:03:32.003 --> 00:03:34.923
they talked to us, they shook our hands
and they built a whole court for us.

00:03:35.423 --> 00:03:38.801
- Just to see the excitement
and the joy that the kids had.

00:03:38.927 --> 00:03:41.095
- That makes an impact even after we leave.

00:03:41.179 --> 00:03:44.557
I mean, we pull up to cities and we play
some basketball and we have conversations

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:45.558
and then we go on to the next city.

00:03:46.017 --> 00:03:48.937
But I think that we were able to really make a
lasting impact in that community in Oak Cliff.

00:03:55.443 --> 00:03:56.945
- Being in Atlanta has been amazing.

00:03:57.028 --> 00:04:00.782
It was definitely one of the spots we were looking
across the map like, where do we want to stop?

00:04:00.823 --> 00:04:02.283
It was Atlanta 100 percent.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:05.745
It's a huge, huge culture spot for civil rights.

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:07.372
There's so much history in Atlanta.

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:09.582
First stop we pulled up to was a John Lewis mural.

00:04:09.832 --> 00:04:13.086
And when you stand underneath it and we have
to look up, I mean, you're just in awe of him

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:15.380
and what he represents in civil rights history.

00:04:16.005 --> 00:04:20.218
Stopping by Martin Luther King Jr.'s birth
home and standing on those steps, besides

00:04:20.218 --> 00:04:23.221
just the Hoop Bus being there, I think being
there as an individual was really impactful.

00:04:23.638 --> 00:04:25.098
- This city is the most important to me.

00:04:25.139 --> 00:04:30.270
- Being born Northside Hospital, Atlanta, Georgia,
raised in Marietta, Georgia, literally playing

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:33.106
recreational ball right up there in that gym.

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:35.608
Knowin' all the Black excellence
that is in Atlanta and being able

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:37.485
to bring the Hoop Bus here myself.

00:04:37.652 --> 00:04:41.281
I could tell my daughter years from now,
your father did something positive, beyond

00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:45.243
basketball, something big that will last forever,
that these kids out here will see forever.

00:04:45.243 --> 00:04:47.620
And they'll be like, when I get
older, I need to do that too.

00:04:50.039 --> 00:04:51.541
- Everybody put their fists in.

00:04:51.874 --> 00:04:52.709
We're in this together.

00:04:52.709 --> 00:04:54.043
We came a long way together.

00:04:54.085 --> 00:04:59.507
- The march taking place here in Washington, 57
years to the day after Martin Luther King Jr.

00:04:59.507 --> 00:05:01.009
gave his "I Have a Dream" speech.

00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:04.679
- If you're looking for a savior,
get up and find a mirror.

00:05:05.054 --> 00:05:08.516
We must become the heroes of
the history we are making.

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:14.355
- To come to Washington, to be able to
walk in the shoes behind the trailblazers

00:05:14.397 --> 00:05:19.193
like Martin Luther King, 57th anniversary
for I Have a Dream, is amazing.

00:05:19.444 --> 00:05:25.283
- The Freedom Riders that were in 1961 really
showed that example of standing for something.

00:05:25.325 --> 00:05:26.409
- Let’s finish this together.

00:05:26.409 --> 00:05:27.535
It's not over.

00:05:27.535 --> 00:05:28.786
- The people have the power.

00:05:28.786 --> 00:05:30.872
When we gather together, we can do anything.

00:05:30.913 --> 00:05:31.622
Build courts.

00:05:31.956 --> 00:05:35.960
- We dedicate a court, a court
that has a nod to the great

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:37.837
Dr. Martin Luther King Jr.

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:40.089
- Change communities.

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:43.259
- We want to see change happen,
and we want to see justice.

00:05:43.926 --> 00:05:45.136
We won't rest until we do.

00:05:45.386 --> 00:05:50.183
- There is a knee upon the neck of
democracy, and our nation can only live

00:05:50.224 --> 00:05:53.102
so long without the oxygen of freedom.

00:05:53.311 --> 00:05:58.274
- I have a dream as well to, you know, help change
the world and to make the world a better place.

00:05:58.274 --> 00:05:59.567
- Black lives!

00:05:59.567 --> 00:06:00.818
- Matter!

00:06:01.069 --> 00:06:05.615
- The strength must be exercised by more
than rhetoric and more than marching.

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:08.743
- It's a full global civil rights movement.

00:06:08.785 --> 00:06:10.328
- We're on this journey together.

00:06:10.661 --> 00:06:13.081
It's not over 57 years later.

00:06:13.164 --> 00:06:14.248
Still a lot of work to be done.

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:18.795
- As the civil rights movement is moving
forward, the Hoop Bus is following.

00:06:18.878 --> 00:06:20.505
- We have only just begun.

00:06:20.505 --> 00:06:22.507
- Our journey has not ended yet.

00:06:22.757 --> 00:06:25.468
We will continue amplifying
the voices of the unheard.

00:06:25.635 --> 00:06:27.303
- It’s not a moment at all.

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:32.850
- Going into the communities and let the world know
that these are the people that make America great.

00:06:32.934 --> 00:06:33.935
- "Carry on" on three.

00:06:34.143 --> 00:06:36.479
One, two, three: Carry on!

